Just in case you guys haven't seen it, DBpedia: http://dbpedia.org/About

The idea there is to scrape structured information out of the infoboxes. If 
each gismu had an infobox with the gloss words, rafsi, definition, etc. and 
perhaps each sumti place separately, DBpedia may have software that will 
automate scraping it.

It would also be a push towards RDF, which is probably a good idea anyway 
since the crux of RDF is ontologies and that's exactly what Lojban's 
vocabulary is.
 

